<article class="env-remark" id="0499">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0499">Remark <span data-tag="0499">8.1.6.9</span>.</a> In the situation of Proposition <a data-tag="0496" href="/tag/0496">8.1.6.7</a>, let $\sigma $ be an $n$-simplex of the $\infty $-bicategory $\operatorname{Cospan}^{L,R}(\operatorname{\mathcal{C}})$, corresponding to a diagram </p>
<div class="equation" id="049A">
<span class="equation-label"><a data-tag="049A" href="/tag/049A">8.19</a></span>
<div>\begin{equation}  \begin{gathered}\label{pith-of-cospan} \xymatrix@R =40pt@C=20pt{ X_{0,0} \ar [dr] &amp;  &amp;  X_{1,1} \ar [dr] \ar [dl] &amp;  \cdots &amp;  X_{n-1,n-1} \ar [dr] \ar [dl] &amp;  &amp;  X_{n,n} \ar [dl] \\ &amp;  \cdots \ar [dr] &amp;  &amp;  \cdots \ar [dr] \ar [dl] &amp;  &amp;  \cdots \ar [dl] &amp;  \\ &amp;  &amp;  X_{0,n-1} \ar [dr] &amp;  &amp;  X_{1,n} \ar [dl] &amp;  &amp;  \\ &amp;  &amp;  &amp;  X_{0,n} &amp;  &amp;  &amp;  \\ } \end{gathered} \end{equation}</div>
</div>
<p> in the $\infty $-category $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$. Then $\sigma $ is contained in the pith $\operatorname{Pith}( \operatorname{Cospan}^{L,R}( \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}) )$ if and only if each of the rectangular regions in the diagram (<a data-tag="049A" href="/tag/049A">8.19</a>) is a pushout square in the $\infty $-category $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$. This follows from the thinness criterion of Corollary <a data-tag="0498" href="/tag/0498">8.1.6.8</a> (together with Proposition <a data-tag="03FZ" href="/tag/03FZ">7.6.2.40</a>). </p>
</article>
